From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:24:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add Exclude BitTorrent setting

Port of the forkop setting (forkop #72, also in Gavr1024/forkop-mod).

New settings.exclude_bittorrent (default off). When enabled, sniffed
BitTorrent/DHT traffic is routed to bypass-out right after sniffing and
before any section rule, so torrent clients keep working without being
proxied. HTTP/HTTPS trackers still follow section rules. The option is
part of the sing-box runtime signature, so toggling it regenerates the
config.

Both Russian catalogs (po/ru and fe-app-trafira/locales) get the new
strings and stay identical; generated calls.json and .pot templates are
not touched (the LuCI package only builds po/ru).

Checked with sing-box 1.12.22, 1.14.2 and 1.14.1-extended
(`sing-box check`, tests/exclude_bittorrent.sh).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
